  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Seoul ODA Challenge</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Policy Advisory and Pilot Project on Urban Traffic Management in Lima, PeruThis project aims to conduct a comprehensive analysis of the traffic conditions in Lima, Peru, and provide policy advisory services for the establishment of a centralized traffic signal and control center. It also includes advisory support for the development and implementation of automated enforcement systems, along with the creation of a test bed to verify and assess the effectiveness of the proposed solutions. Furthermore, seminars will be held at the inception, mid-term, and final stages of the project, complemented by capacity-building programs designed to strengthen the capabilities of local stakeholders and support the sustainable adoption of an integrated traffic management system. Formulation of the Urban Master Plan for Phnom Penh, CambodiaThis project focuses on systematically assessing the pedestrian environment along Preaengeng Street in Phnom Penh, Cambodia, and developing a concept plan to create a pedestrian-friendly corridor. Based on this analysis, policy recommendations and an actionable implementation plan will be formulated, reflecting local needs and urban characteristics. Additionally, knowledge exchange activities will be carried out to share advanced pedestrian policies and design methodologies between Korea and Cambodia, while training and workshops will be conducted to enhance the capacity of local stakeholders and establish a foundation for sustainable urban planning. Pre-Feasibility Study for the Establishment of a Waste Treatment Facility in Colombo, Sri LankaThis project seeks to undertake a thorough assessment of Sri Lankas current waste management conditions and analyze the technical and economic pre-feasibility of establishing a biogas facility utilizing organic waste. It also involves examining the institutional and financial environment required to promote private investment projects and developing related policy and implementation measures. In addition, capacity-building workshops and invitational training programs will be organized for local decision-makers and technical personnel to enhance expertise in waste management and lay the groundwork for sustainable project development.</narrative>
  </description>
